Done. Created the TMP102 Zig 0.16 project in `artifacts/tmp102/prompt0c/`.

**`src/root.zig`** — conversion functions + reference algorithms (imported as the shared `prompt0c` module), all verified by `zig build test` (passes):
- Byte order: `bytesToWord` / `wordToBytes` (I²C big-endian)
- Normal 12-bit temp: `decodeTempNormal` / `encodeTempNormal` (left-aligned bits 15:4)
- Extended 13-bit temp: `decodeTempExtended` / `encodeTempExtended` (bits 15:3 + bit-0 EM marker)
- Config register: `getBit`/`setBit`, `configShutdown/ExtendedMode/Polarity/ThermostatMode`, `conversionRateField/Hz`, `faultQueueCount`

**`src/main.zig`** — demo (`21.0 C -> register 0x1500, decoded 21.00 C`).

**`conversions_manifest.md`** — per-function worked examples + exact bit-layout assumptions.

**`feedback/tmp102/prompt0c.md`** — notes the spec's extended-mode `0x0960` is a 13-bit count, not a register word; resolved against the raw datasheet (bits 15:3 + bit-0 marker).

One note: the spec's extended-mode example was ambiguous, so I implemented the datasheet layout (Tables 6-8/6-9) and documented the discrepancy in the manifest.
